  </div>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">The type and rule above prints on all proofs including departmental reproduction proofs. MUST be removed before printing.</p>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">If your salary is not subject to withholding, or if you are self-employed, you may be able to deduct the amount you paid in 2005 for medical expenses and health insurance coverage for your spouse, and your yourself.</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">Generally, you must estimate your tax, making sure you pay enough tax throughout the year. If you pay too little, you may be subject to penalties for not paying enough tax as you earn income.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">More information.</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">For more information on filing your return, including when and where to file, see the instructions for Form 1040.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Filing Your Return</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">You have to file an income tax return for 2005 if your gross income was at least the amount shown in the third column of Table A.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">Additional requirements. Even if your income was less than the amount shown in Table A, you may still have to file a return if you have certain other types of income or if you are required to file for other reasons.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Retirement Savings Arrangements</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">Retirement savings arrangements are plans that allow you to save for your retirement. You can contribute to a traditional IRA or a Roth IRA. You can also contribute to a traditional IRA may be tax-deductible, depending on your income and whether you are covered by a workplace retirement plan (like a 401(k)).</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">For more information on IRAs, see Publication 590-B.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Self-employment tax.</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">If you are self-employed, you must pay self-employment tax. This tax is a combination of Social Security and Medicare taxes. You can deduct one-half of your self-employment tax from your gross income.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">If you are self-employed, you must also report your net earnings from self-employment on Schedule C (Form 1040).</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Retirement plans for the self-employed.</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">If you are self-employed, you may be able to contribute to a self-employed retirement plan. These plans allow you to save for retirement and may be tax-deductible. Some plans are available only to self-employed individuals.</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">For more information on IRAs, see Publication 590-B.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-bottom: 10px;">Exception from SE tax.</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">If you are a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of poverty, you may be exempt from paying self-employment tax on the income received for services performed as an agent of the order.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
